 "elapsed_s": 17.2,
 "text": "If you call yourself an AI engineer without knowing how to build custom agents, then you'll probably be left behind. And what I mean by AI agents is not Hermes or Open Claw, but custom agents are AI agents that you build from scratch. Now, you don't have to write any line of code. You can do it using GPT or Cloud, but you still have to define the logic, the architecture. The tools and the skills yourself for the agent. And think of it like this. If you join a company and you want to automate a process or they just ask you to build an agent for a certain task, then this one needs to be custom because you cannot give them a Hermes or an Open Claw agent. You don't even know what it will do, so you'd have to build your own custom agent with what you're trying to automate. And with this approach, what it is better than having an Hermes or Open Claw, it is that these type of agents are very thin, so they are not heavy, but still customizable and flexible and can handle at scale, which the heavy Hermes or Open Claw agent cannot do at scale.",
